WEBVTT

00:00.150 --> 00:06.130
Phobos is the innermost and larger of the two natural satellites of Mars, the other being Deimos.

00:06.615 --> 00:11.975
The two moons were discovered in 1877 by American astronomer Asaph Hall.

00:12.602 --> 00:20.243
Phobos is named after the Greek god of fear and panic, who is the twin brother of Deimos and son of Ares (Mars).
